; it-passthrough — one of everything the IT core never decodes.
;
; An instrument body, three samples (PCM, IT215-compressed and ModPlug
; ADPCM — three different ways of deciding where the data ENDS), a
; foreign trailing chunk another tracker wrote, and tempura's own `TMPU`
; payload. Rung 2 compares every one of those regions as BYTES against
; its own anchor: pass-through means the bytes come back, not that the
; offsets do.
(read)
(roundtrip)
